{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, a number is to be written at each of the vertices of the three pentagons. Some of the numbers have already been written.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If the sum of the numbers at the vertices of each pentagon is to be 25, what is thevalue of x?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5ecd488cadab6008fa2f28c05d03b86ffa207e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see the sum of the other unknown side lengths must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1ba9639368fe40e4d70d8adb8797c0e600322c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(25 - 5 - 9 - 4) + (25 - 7 - 3 - 7) = (25 - 18) + (25 - 17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"468\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/431a6b9b403114e75674adfb4f251d5deba50c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + 8= 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9709ebe345b2056b867e7b01a8f60822967a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 25 - 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f44383cda95695b7b388e5eeaba3eb18c528525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=